      "tests": [
        "lake build AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ActualProjectedRotation"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel base E with canonical volume, including the disclosed rank-zero extension; V is C²; 0<α≤β; both global Hessian bounds; η>0 and βη≤1.",
        "Canonical normalized laws/kernel, onto pullback e, SAME U/T, full and centered roots, exact centering, gap, unit and bounded inverse are conclusions. Conditional actions are per-observable AE. L² is not assumed finite-dimensional.",
        "γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη); the inverse acts only on H_P^0=ker⟨e1,·⟩ with inherited Hilbert structure; the legal endpoint αη=1 is retained.",
        "H_perp is exactly ker P (conditional expectation given Y), while H_P^0 is the zero ν-mean macroscopic space. Their complete Hilbert structures, B_0 and V_0 are internally constructed; no onto-kerP or coisometry assumption is introduced.",
        "The concluded global-input implication quantifies every f∈L²(J) with integral zero. R,conditional centering,constant annihilation,adjoint range and norm decomposition are derived internally. Private statement definitions expand literally to the original sealed propositions and add no premise.",
        "The global output mean, actual projected component formulas and pair-energy identity are internally proved conclusions. There is no additional zero-output-mean, onto-V0, sharp-energy or higher-smoothness hypothesis."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive operator Γ on the real scalar-valued L² space with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. There is q∈L²(ν;ℝ) equal to one ν-almost everywhere, with Tq=q and ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for every u. Set q_P=e q and H_P^0=ker⟨q_P,·⟩, with its inherited Hilbert structure. Membership is exactly zero ν-mean after e⁻¹. The SAME Γ_P annihilates q_P. Put γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη)>0. There exists Γ_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 equal under inclusion to the restriction of Γ_P, positive with Γ_0−γ I positive. Γ_0 is a unit in the algebra of bounded real operators. There exists a bounded real Inv on this SAME centered space with Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. All probability, normalization, range, root, centering, spectral-gap, unit and inverse facts are internally derived from the original inputs; none is an additional public premise. αη=1 and rank-zero E remain legal. No inverse on full H_P is asserted. Define the actual closed conditional-mean-zero space H_perp=ker P in L²(J;ℝ), with its inherited complete Hilbert structure; this is not merely the globally zero-mean joint space. There exists B_0:H_P^0→H_perp whose inclusion equals B i_0. There exists V_0:H_P^0→H_perp with V_0=B_0 Inv, B_0=V_0 Γ_0, V_0* V_0=I and ‖V_0 f‖=‖f‖ for every f∈H_P^0. All these objects and identities are conclusions from the same original inputs. There exists the canonical bounded residual map R:L²(J;ℝ)→H_perp with i_perp Rg=g−Pg for every joint g. The SAME ambient adjoint satisfies B* g=i_0 B_0* Rg for every joint g; the printed intrinsic block adjoint is recovered on H_perp. For every actual joint f∈L²(J;ℝ) with ∫f dJ=0, there exists f_P∈H_P^0 whose inclusion is E[f|Y]. Put f_perp=Rf and f_V=V_0* f_perp∈the SAME H_P^0. Then B* i_perp f_perp=i_0 Γ_0 f_V=Γ_P i_0 f_V, ‖f‖²=‖f_P‖²+‖f_perp‖² and ‖f_V‖≤‖f_perp‖. The global zero-mean condition is a quantified input restriction to this concluded implication, not an extra assumption on the potential or an operator certificate. The SAME root commutes with T and its transport commutes with A. The SAME Inv on H_P^0 is selfadjoint. There exists an internally constructed A_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 whose inclusion equals A after inclusion; it is selfadjoint,commutes with Γ_0,satisfies A_0²+Γ_0²=I,and commutes with the SAME Inv. For the same U,R and inclusion of H_perp=ker P, define D=R U inclusion. Its full-domain identity V0*D=-A0 V0* is retained. For EVERY globally mean-zero f in L2(J), let fP be its actual centered conditional-expectation component, fperp=R f and fV=V0* fperp. Define the actual output g=U(P f-(f-P f)), not an abstract pair chosen to satisfy a matrix identity. The theorem proves its global mean is zero internally from invariance of the actual reflected augmentation law and preservation of the integral by conditional expectation. Let gP be the actual centered conditional-expectation component of this SAME g, gperp=R g and gV=V0* gperp. Then gP=A0 fP-Gamma0 fV, gV=Gamma0 fP+A0 fV, and ||gP||^2+||gV||^2=||fP||^2+||fV||^2. Both output components are produced by these actual conditional/polar semantics before proving the formulas; neither is defined as its right-hand side. All previous law/kernel/root/inverse/polar/full-micro and centered-observable conclusions persist with the SAME twelve witnesses and the original six analytic caller conditions. No surjectivity, sharp-energy68 bound, extra regularity or zero-output-mean premise is introduced. One private literal Prop stores the complete sealed mathematical conclusion; it supplies no proof provider or additional hypothesis. The actual B21 corrector change, B4 dynamics, weak H1/B2, main convergence, invariance/nonexplosion, implementation errors/caps, expected-query costs and actual-input composition remain separate obligations.",
      "formula": "g=U(Pf-(f-Pf)),\\quad g_P=A_0f_P-\\Gamma_0f_V,\\quad g_V=\\Gamma_0f_P+A_0f_V,\\quad \\|g_P\\|^2+\\|g_V\\|^2=\\|f_P\\|^2+\\|f_V\\|^2.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Retain the same actual probability geometry and operators",
          "text": "Unfold the literal proposition and apply the independently accepted original-input parent. Retain its actual law, conditional kernel, reflection, centered defect root, inverse, polar isometry and globally centered-observable decomposition. The complete macro and micro subspaces have their inherited Hilbert structures.",
          "formula": "H_P^0=\\ker\\langle q_P,\\cdot\\rangle,\\quad H_\\perp=\\ker P,\\quad Rf=f-Pf.",
          "lean": "  unfold actual_projected_rotation_statement\n  classical\n  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n  let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n    (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n  let ν := J.snd\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n  letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) := ⟨measurable_snd.comap_le⟩\n  let HP := lpMeas ℝ ℝ mY 2 J\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP := HP.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP := HP.innerProductSpace\n  let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    HP.subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ := J) measurable_snd.comap_le\n  have hBase := AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ReflectionIntertwining.actual_reflection_intertwining\n    (E:=E) (V:=V) (α:=α) (β:=β) (η:=η) hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  have parentSlice0 := hBase\n  have hμ := parentSlice0.1\n  have parentSlice1 := parentSlice0.2\n  have hJ := parentSlice1.1\n  have parentSlice2 := parentSlice1.2\n  have hν := parentSlice2.1\n  have parentSlice3 := parentSlice2.2\n  have hRange := parentSlice3.1\n  have parentSlice4 := parentSlice3.2\n  have hPf := parentSlice4.1\n  have parentSlice5 := parentSlice4.2\n  obtain ⟨S, parentSlice6⟩ := parentSlice5\n  have hS := parentSlice6.1\n  have parentSlice7 := parentSlice6.2\n  have hSd := parentSlice7.1\n  have parentSlice8 := parentSlice7.2\n  have hSc := parentSlice8.1\n  have parentSlice9 := parentSlice8.2\n  have hSf := parentSlice9.1\n  have parentSlice10 := parentSlice9.2\n  have hSs := parentSlice10.1\n  have parentSlice11 := parentSlice10.2\n  obtain ⟨e, parentSlice12⟩ := parentSlice11\n  have he := parentSlice12.1\n  have parentSlice13 := parentSlice12.2\n  obtain ⟨U, parentSlice14⟩ := parentSlice13\n  have hU := parentSlice14.1\n  have parentSlice15 := parentSlice14.2\n  have hUi := parentSlice15.1\n  have parentSlice16 := parentSlice15.2\n  have hUs := parentSlice16.1\n  have parentSlice17 := parentSlice16.2\n  obtain ⟨T, parentSlice18⟩ := parentSlice17\n  have hTs := parentSlice18.1\n  have parentSlice19 := parentSlice18.2\n  have hAll := parentSlice19.1\n  have parentSlice20 := parentSlice19.2\n  have hAeq := parentSlice20.1\n  have parentSlice21 := parentSlice20.2\n  have hAs := parentSlice21.1\n  have parentSlice22 := parentSlice21.2\n  have hAn := parentSlice22.1\n  have parentSlice23 := parentSlice22.2\n  have hPB := parentSlice23.1\n  have parentSlice24 := parentSlice23.2\n  obtain ⟨Γ, parentSlice25⟩ := parentSlice24\n  have hΓ := parentSlice25.1\n  have parentSlice26 := parentSlice25.2\n  have hΓSq := parentSlice26.1\n  have parentSlice27 := parentSlice26.2\n  have hCommRoot := parentSlice27.1\n  have parentSlice28 := parentSlice27.2\n  have hΓP := parentSlice28.1\n  have parentSlice29 := parentSlice28.2\n  have hΓPSq := parentSlice29.1\n  have parentSlice30 := parentSlice29.2\n  have hCommP := parentSlice30.1\n  have parentSlice31 := parentSlice30.2\n  have hGram := parentSlice31.1\n  have parentSlice32 := parentSlice31.2\n  obtain ⟨q, parentSlice33⟩ := parentSlice32\n  have hqa := parentSlice33.1\n  have parentSlice34 := parentSlice33.2\n  have hTq := parentSlice34.1\n  have parentSlice35 := parentSlice34.2\n  have hq := parentSlice35.1\n  have parentSlice36 := parentSlice35.2\n  have hCenter := parentSlice36.1\n  have parentSlice37 := parentSlice36.2\n  have hΓPq := parentSlice37.1\n  have parentSlice38 := parentSlice37.2\n  have hγ := parentSlice38.1\n  have parentSlice39 := parentSlice38.2\n  obtain ⟨ΓP0, parentSlice40⟩ := parentSlice39\n  have hΓP0 := parentSlice40.1\n  have parentSlice41 := parentSlice40.2\n  have hPos0 := parentSlice41.1\n  have parentSlice42 := parentSlice41.2\n  have hOrder0 := parentSlice42.1\n  have parentSlice43 := parentSlice42.2\n  have hUnit := parentSlice43.1\n  have parentSlice44 := parentSlice43.2\n  obtain ⟨Inv, parentSlice45⟩ := parentSlice44\n  have hLeft := parentSlice45.1\n  have parentSlice46 := parentSlice45.2\n  have hRight := parentSlice46.1\n  have parentSlice47 := parentSlice46.2\n  have hNormInv := parentSlice47.1\n  have parentSlice48 := parentSlice47.2\n  have hInvSelf := parentSlice48.1\n  have parentSlice49 := parentSlice48.2\n  obtain ⟨A0, parentSlice50⟩ := parentSlice49\n  have hA0 := parentSlice50.1\n  have parentSlice51 := parentSlice50.2\n  have hA0self := parentSlice51.1\n  have parentSlice52 := parentSlice51.2\n  have hComm0 := parentSlice52.1\n  have parentSlice53 := parentSlice52.2\n  have hSquare0 := parentSlice53.1\n  have parentSlice54 := parentSlice53.2\n  have hCommInv := parentSlice54.1\n  have parentSlice55 := parentSlice54.2\n  obtain ⟨B0, parentSlice56⟩ := parentSlice55\n  have hB0 := parentSlice56.1\n  have parentSlice57 := parentSlice56.2\n  obtain ⟨V0, parentSlice58⟩ := parentSlice57\n  have hVdef := parentSlice58.1\n  have parentSlice59 := parentSlice58.2\n  have hFactor := parentSlice59.1\n  have parentSlice60 := parentSlice59.2\n  have hVadj := parentSlice60.1\n  have parentSlice61 := parentSlice60.2\n  have hVnorm := parentSlice61.1\n  have parentSlice62 := parentSlice61.2\n  obtain ⟨R, parentSlice63⟩ := parentSlice62\n  have hR := parentSlice63.1\n  have parentSlice64 := parentSlice63.2\n  have hAmbient := parentSlice64.1\n  have parentSlice65 := parentSlice64.2\n  have hDparent := parentSlice65.1\n  have parentSlice66 := parentSlice65.2\n  have hIntertwineParent := parentSlice66.1\n  have hGlobal := parentSlice66.2\n  let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP := HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P) ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n  let qP : HP := e q\n  let HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP0 := HP0.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP0 := HP0.innerProductSpace\n  letI : CompleteSpace HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n  let Hperp := P.ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup Hperp := Hperp.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ Hperp := Hperp.innerProductSpace\n  letI : CompleteSpace Hperp := P.isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n  change HP0 →L[ℝ] Hperp at B0 V0\n  change HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 at ΓP0 Inv A0\n  change Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Hperp at R\n  change (∀ g : Lp ℝ 2 J, (R g : Lp ℝ 2 J)=g-P g) at hR\n  change (∀ g : Lp ℝ 2 J,\n    B.adjoint g=HP0.subtypeL (B0.adjoint (R g))) at hAmbient\n  change (∀ f : Lp ℝ 2 J, (∫ z, f z ∂J)=0 →\n    ∃ fP : HP0,\n      HP0.subtypeL fP=condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ:=J) measurable_snd.comap_le f ∧\n      let fperp : Hperp := R f\n      let fV : HP0 := V0.adjoint fperp\n      B.adjoint (fperp : Lp ℝ 2 J)=HP0.subtypeL (ΓP0 fV) ∧\n      HP0.subtypeL (ΓP0 fV)=ΓP (HP0.subtypeL fV) ∧\n      ‖f‖^2=‖fP‖^2+‖fperp‖^2 ∧ ‖fV‖≤‖fperp‖) at hGlobal\n",
          "detail": "Exact compiled BODY span; preceding local definitions and inherited Hilbert structures stay in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualProjectedRotation.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "03a0721ae952f744d0bfdf568039b77f7035bec0a50642f8bc8ebc895273b998",
