is exactly the normalized exponential tilt of volume by\n  x -> -V((y+x)/2) - ||y-x||^2/(8*eta).\nIt is a conditional kernel for Lambda, namely the conditional law of the second coordinate given the first, and both marginals of Lambda equal nu. The every-y equality of measures is stronger in scope than a merely nu-almost-everywhere description of the kernel.\n\ne:K -> HP is a surjective real-linear isometry (an isometric linear equivalence), and for every u in K its inclusion into H equals M u. U:H -> H is a real-linear isometry whose representative action for each g in H is U g = g composed with F, J-almost everywhere. U is involutive and its bounded linear map is selfadjoint. The exceptional null set in the displayed representative equality may depend on g.\n\nT:K -> K is bounded real-linear and selfadjoint. For every u in K, simultaneously,\n  ||T u|| <= ||u||,\n  T u(y) = integral u(x) dS(y)(x), for nu-almost every y,\n  integral T u dnu = integral u dnu.\nThe kernel-action equality is an equality of representatives almost everywhere for each observable u; a single common exceptional set for all u is not asserted.\n\nDefine A:HP -> HP by orthogonally projecting U restricted to HP back onto HP. Define B:HP -> H by (I-P) U P after inclusion of HP into H. Then\n  A = e T e^(-1),\n  A is selfadjoint, and ||A f|| <= ||f|| for every f in HP,\n  P(B f)=0 for every f in HP.\nHere and below multiplication of endomorphisms is composition, adjoints are Hilbert adjoints, and all operator equalities are exact equalities of bounded linear maps.\n\nGamma:K -> K is bounded real-linear, positive, satisfies Gamma^2=I-T^2, and commutes with T. Positivity includes selfadjointness and nonnegative quadratic form. Set GammaP=e Gamma e^(-1):HP -> HP. Then GammaP is positive, GammaP^2=I-A^2, GammaP commutes with A, and B^* B=GammaP^2 as operators on HP.\n\nq is an element of K represented nu-almost everywhere by the constant function 1. It satisfies T q=q, and for every u in K,\n  <q,u>